# Schedules for the scheduler container (supercronic, standard cron syntax, UTC).
# Collectors are added here as they land; each one fetches any days it missed.

# Every hour: confirm the database and object storage are reachable.
0 * * * * dr check

# Every day at 04:30 UTC: SEAP direct purchases finalized up to yesterday.
30 4 * * * dr collect seap-direct

# Every day at 05:30 UTC: SEAP award notices published up to yesterday, with the
# contracts, winners, detail and versions of each (three requests or more per notice,
# a few minutes a day).
30 5 * * * dr collect seap-awards

# Every day at 07:30 UTC: the detail and versions of the notices that a failed request
# left without them. Nothing to ask for on most days.
30 7 * * * dr collect seap-award-details

# Every day at 08:30 UTC, after the SEAP jobs: ANAF's record (county and locality) of the
# institutions and companies they brought that ANAF was not asked about yet, 100 tax IDs
# a call, then every entity placed again. A few calls on most days, none when nothing
# is new.
30 8 * * * dr collect anaf

# Not scheduled, on purpose: `pnias-payments` and `seap-exports` read files that appear
# about monthly and quarterly, and a new payment file also needs `dr reparse seap-exports`
# for its new builders. They are run by hand for now; whether they join this file is an
# open todo in the workspace notes.
